WEBVTT

00:01.100 --> 00:03.560
Mother, please tell me.

00:03.560 --> 00:07.570
What traits of Father did you come to like?

00:07.570 --> 00:12.070
Have you ever felt anxious, been doubtful of him or had quarrels with him?

00:12.070 --> 00:14.910
Even though the skies of Greece are so blue,

00:14.910 --> 00:17.370
a downpour of rain falls over my heart.

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
NAAJA

00:26.420 --> 00:27.710
Nadja,

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
With your eyes

00:27.840 --> 00:30.380
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
Nadja,

00:30.380 --> 00:31.590
NAAJA

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
What do you see?

00:31.630 --> 00:33.880
Nani ga mieru

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Shining in the far distance,

00:33.930 --> 00:36.800
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
The door to the future,

00:36.800 --> 00:39.180
Mirai no tobira

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
That's what I'm searching for

00:40.100 --> 00:43.560
Sagashite iru

00:43.560 --> 00:50.780
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:51.480 --> 00:54.990
Minna egao de aetara

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:55.070 --> 00:58.320
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
It could be so much more fun

00:58.370 --> 01:01.580
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:01.620 --> 01:05.040
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.420 --> 01:08.710
Tabi no owari wa mienai

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
God is the only one who could possibly know

01:08.840 --> 01:12.170
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:12.340 --> 01:15.930
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
I will go waving

01:15.970 --> 01:18.090
Te wo furinagara

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.180 --> 01:24.850
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
But I won't look back

01:24.890 --> 01:27.600
Ushiro mukanai

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Until the day my dream comes true

01:27.940 --> 01:32.900
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
Nadja, Your smile

01:33.190 --> 01:36.610
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
Nadja, gives me courage

01:36.700 --> 01:40.030
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Under the blue sky,

01:40.070 --> 01:42.990
Aoi sora no shita de

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
I will find the place

01:43.120 --> 01:45.960
Ashita no yukue

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
where my future lies

01:46.250 --> 01:50.170
Mitsukeru kara

02:11.880 --> 02:14.750
﻿Abel! The tea's ready!

02:14.760 --> 02:15.920
﻿I'll be right there!

02:17.090 --> 02:19.630
﻿Oh? What are you making?

02:20.800 --> 02:22.010
﻿A nutcracker doll.

02:22.640 --> 02:24.140
﻿A nutcracker doll?

02:24.140 --> 02:26.270
﻿Yes. They're dolls made for families.

02:27.180 --> 02:30.190
But... why is the father the only one with no face on it?

02:37.650 --> 02:39.110
﻿Mind your own business.

02:49.190 --> 02:54.190
The Pierrot who Won't Cry

04:03.360 --> 04:06.070
﻿Hello, everyone!

04:10.500 --> 04:13.000
﻿Oh, pardon me. Could you please let us through?

04:15.210 --> 04:16.210
﻿Here we go!

04:24.010 --> 04:26.720
﻿You should be able to see it well from here, Stefan.

04:27.200 --> 04:27.660
Yeah!

04:28.510 --> 04:29.470
﻿Stefan?!

04:29.850 --> 04:31.310
﻿O-Oops!

04:33.600 --> 04:35.190
﻿Isn't that great, Stefan?

04:38.440 --> 04:39.440
﻿Mary!

04:56.790 --> 04:58.130
﻿Granny, hurry and start the music!

04:58.130 --> 04:59.340
Sure thing.

05:15.020 --> 05:16.890
﻿Oh, Mr. Pierrot!

05:16.900 --> 05:21.820
﻿Here you already have me! Oh! Yet still, you stare at another pretty lady.

05:21.820 --> 05:23.070
﻿Unforgivable!

05:24.610 --> 05:27.910
﻿I have no choice but to give you a severe punishment!

05:28.450 --> 05:29.450
﻿Is he all right?!

05:29.450 --> 05:31.740
﻿Follow me. I'm taking him to a doctor.

05:31.740 --> 05:33.580
﻿Kennosuke, switch with me onstage!

05:33.580 --> 05:34.540
﻿Okay!

05:42.880 --> 05:46.170
﻿It looks like it was just a slight concussion. Everything else seems to be normal.

05:46.550 --> 05:47.840
﻿Thank goodness.

05:48.260 --> 05:50.970
﻿Sorry for making you all worry like that, everyone.

05:50.970 --> 05:54.770
﻿You hardly ever make mistakes Abel, so we were all really surprised.

05:56.390 --> 05:58.350
﻿Excuse me, is the troupe leader around?

05:59.350 --> 06:01.190
﻿That would be me.

06:11.370 --> 06:14.330
﻿Everyone, listen to this! We have work tomorrow night too!

06:16.120 --> 06:20.330
﻿That person just now wants us to perform for a floating party he's having.

06:20.920 --> 06:26.380
﻿He saw our show earlier and asked to come to his son's birthday party.

06:26.380 --> 06:29.340
﻿That's the rich for you! The things they do are really something else.

06:29.340 --> 06:34.050
﻿There was a couple in front of the stage who brought their boy in a wheelchair, right?

06:34.390 --> 06:35.560
﻿They hired us.

06:42.860 --> 06:44.960
﻿We're going to be performing on a boat!

06:43.650 --> 06:46.860
﻿That party... I think I'll pass on it.

06:48.780 --> 06:51.990
﻿Is your head injury bothering you after all?

06:51.990 --> 06:53.410
﻿I just don't want to show up there.

06:55.290 --> 06:56.700
﻿What's gotten into you, Abel...?

06:57.620 --> 06:58.790
﻿Abel...

07:00.420 --> 07:04.000
﻿Could it possibly be... because of the family who's holding the part—

07:04.840 --> 07:06.840
﻿Enough already! Please leave me alone!

07:06.840 --> 07:08.010
﻿Abel!

07:12.720 --> 07:15.430
﻿From what it looks like,

07:15.430 --> 07:18.890
﻿the family that hired us is the new family of Abel's divorced wife and son.

07:19.890 --> 07:21.440
﻿So that really was it.

07:21.690 --> 07:26.320
﻿When Abel fell from the ball, it was right when that family came in front of the stage.

07:26.860 --> 07:30.490
﻿Nadja, what's the matter? You haven't touched your plate.

07:30.860 --> 07:32.820
﻿I'm just concerned about Abel...

07:33.780 --> 07:38.290
﻿I just realized, I really don't know anything about him...

07:40.290 --> 07:44.170
﻿The Abel I know always performs his tricks perfectly...

07:44.170 --> 07:47.750
﻿is smart, and is so kind to everyone...

07:48.590 --> 07:51.920
﻿But, that was just a small part of him.

07:52.430 --> 07:56.010
﻿That's because Abel hardly ever talks about himself.

07:56.510 --> 08:01.930
﻿It's just as well. Why don't we tell everyone? About Abel that is.

08:04.690 --> 08:05.730
﻿I guess so...

08:07.570 --> 08:10.650
﻿Abel first came to our troupe...

08:10.650 --> 08:14.910
﻿when we were traveling through Germany during a harsh winter, four years ago...

08:24.120 --> 08:27.710
﻿Umm... are you of the Dandelion Troupe?

08:28.340 --> 08:31.880
﻿Yes... I'm the troupe leader...

08:31.880 --> 08:34.720
﻿My name is Abel Geiger.

08:35.010 --> 08:38.350
I ﻿was wondering if you would let me join your troupe?

08:39.890 --> 08:43.890
﻿With that way you look... it looks like you have some reason behind this.

08:45.060 --> 08:49.360
﻿Actually... I was just released from the penitentiary yesterday.

08:54.450 --> 08:56.160
﻿A-Abel was...

08:56.160 --> 08:57.660
﻿...a criminal?!

08:57.660 --> 09:00.370
﻿Wait until we're done telling the story.

09:00.370 --> 09:05.710
﻿Abel apparently was a doctor in the countryside for five years before that.

09:06.290 --> 09:11.670
﻿It was a very poor village, and apparently before Abel came, there was no other doctor.

09:11.670 --> 09:13.550
﻿Every family was poor,

09:13.550 --> 09:17.630
﻿so he couldn't bring himself to ask anyone to pay him the fee for the medical examinations.

09:17.640 --> 09:20.010
﻿Before long, he became unable to buy anymore medicine...

09:20.010 --> 09:24.100
﻿which left many families with very painful memories.

09:24.100 --> 09:29.560
﻿In that village, an epidemic of illness broke out, and many people died.

09:30.690 --> 09:34.990
﻿And finally, even Abel's son also fell sick to it.

09:36.650 --> 09:38.490
﻿S-So what happened after that?

09:38.740 --> 09:40.620
﻿Mmm. He snuck out in the dead of night,

09:40.620 --> 09:43.330
﻿intending to take medicine from a hospital in a nearby town.

09:43.330 --> 09:45.580
﻿H-He stole it?

09:50.840 --> 09:52.500
﻿It couldn't be helped!

09:52.710 --> 09:54.210
﻿He was being a good father!

09:55.010 --> 09:56.670
﻿But a crime is still a crime.

09:56.670 --> 10:01.180
﻿He saved his son and the other villagers, but he was caught...

10:01.890 --> 10:06.770
﻿But... I wonder why he didn't return to his house after he was released from jail?

10:08.190 --> 10:12.110
﻿If Abel cared about his family that much, why did he come to our troupe?

10:12.110 --> 10:13.020
﻿That's just strange!

10:13.480 --> 10:14.940
﻿That much we don't know...

10:14.940 --> 10:18.780
﻿It's because Abel hasn't spoken a single word about the matter.

10:25.080 --> 10:27.370
﻿Dear, be careful!

10:28.580 --> 10:31.170
﻿You better listen to what your mother says!

10:32.340 --> 10:36.050
﻿Papa, have a safe trip!

10:36.970 --> 10:38.380
﻿Stefan...

10:45.770 --> 10:48.350
﻿He couldn't possibly not want to see his family...

10:48.350 --> 10:52.020
﻿I'm sure his son wants to see him too.

11:12.920 --> 11:17.090
I'm sure the big ship that Master was talking about... is that one!

11:18.050 --> 11:19.550
﻿Good morning!

11:20.220 --> 11:21.880
﻿Is anyone in?

11:22.680 --> 11:23.470
Who's there?

11:24.640 --> 11:26.140
Ah! From yesterday!

11:26.560 --> 11:29.470
﻿So you remembered me. My name is Nadja.

11:29.480 --> 11:34.020
﻿Do you need something? Mama and Ralph are out right now, but...

11:34.020 --> 11:35.610
﻿You're welcome to come up.

11:39.740 --> 11:42.570
﻿Wow... so you're traveling around the world.

11:43.030 --> 11:44.990
﻿Yes. Searching for my mother all the while.

11:46.740 --> 11:50.700
﻿I was brought up in an orphanage, so I thought I didn't have any parents.

11:51.830 --> 11:55.460
﻿But, I found out that my mother is alive somewhere!

11:56.090 --> 12:00.460
﻿I longed to see her, so I joined the troupe you saw me with, and have been traveling all around.

12:01.670 --> 12:03.510
﻿I understand those feelings of yours.

12:05.220 --> 12:07.720
﻿I'm kind of envious of you, Nadja.

12:07.720 --> 12:10.140
﻿Because you're able to travel the world on your own two feet.

12:10.140 --> 12:12.140
﻿allowing you to look for your mother.

12:12.140 --> 12:15.690
Ii wonder if you ought to be... You're able to ride on that big ship after all.

12:17.150 --> 12:19.320
﻿That ship is Ralph's property.

12:19.570 --> 12:20.530
﻿Ralph?

12:20.530 --> 12:22.440
He's Mama's new husband.

12:23.450 --> 12:26.030
﻿I really should be calling him, "Papa”, but...

12:27.910 --> 12:30.540
Ah, could you please keep this a a secret from my mom?

12:30.540 --> 12:31.580
Sure.

12:31.580 --> 12:34.670
﻿Stefan, do you not like your new father?

12:34.670 --> 12:38.340
﻿That's not it. Ralph's a really good person.

12:39.750 --> 12:44.170
﻿But to me, I'm content with mv one and only father, Abel Geiger.

12:46.050 --> 12:48.600
﻿So you still love your real father then?

12:51.770 --> 12:52.640
﻿I see!

12:52.980 --> 12:58.520
﻿After all, he went as far to commit that crime to save my life!

12:58.520 --> 13:01.480
﻿I think that Mama, too, still loves him even now.

13:01.480 --> 13:05.740
﻿She was always blaming herself, saying it was her fault that he left.

13:06.390 --> 13:07.930
I see.

13:07.930 --> 13:09.990
﻿I see!

13:09.990 --> 13:13.620
But... she remarried, right?

13:13.620 --> 13:16.870
﻿Yeah... but, Papa was at fault too.

13:16.870 --> 13:20.790
﻿Ever since he went missing 4 years ago, he never came back once...

13:20.800 --> 13:23.050
﻿Me and Mama were waiting for him the entire time!

13:24.300 --> 13:27.800
﻿I wonder if Papa really just abandoned us in the end.

13:27.800 --> 13:29.050
﻿That's not true!

13:29.850 --> 13:31.220
﻿It can't possibly be true!

13:38.380 --> 13:39.590
Go get your head on straight.

13:44.720 --> 13:45.380
Huh?

13:47.450 --> 13:48.570
﻿W-Wait here a sec!

13:49.450 --> 13:50.490
﻿Are you all right?

13:51.080 --> 13:51.970
﻿Abel.

13:51.970 --> 13:53.770
N-Nadja?

13:56.790 --> 13:58.120
﻿Save me, Nadja!!

13:58.400 --> 13:59.170
Stefan!

13:59.170 --> 14:00.540
﻿S-Stefan?!

14:00.540 --> 14:01.460
﻿Save me!!

14:01.460 --> 14:02.340
Stefan!!
Save me!!

14:03.500 --> 14:06.300
﻿Uwaaah! Save meeee!!

14:06.300 --> 14:07.470
﻿Stefan!

14:09.660 --> 14:10.930
﻿Stefan!

14:11.800 --> 14:12.580
﻿Stefan?

14:12.580 --> 14:13.240
Papa!

14:13.810 --> 14:14.810
﻿Stefan!

14:23.730 --> 14:25.690
﻿Ungh... S-Stefan...

14:25.690 --> 14:26.900
﻿Arce you all right?!

14:26.900 --> 14:29.860
﻿I'm fine. You should go tend to Papa instead.

14:32.160 --> 14:33.240
﻿Are you all right?

14:33.450 --> 14:35.930
﻿I hit my arm a little hard...

14:35.930 --> 14:36.770
Abe-- Shh!

14:41.040 --> 14:43.040
﻿You're that pierrot from last night, aren't you?

14:43.040 --> 14:44.840
﻿Please let me take a look at it.

14:45.760 --> 14:47.550
﻿It seems like the bone has been fractured.

14:49.930 --> 14:53.680
﻿All right, I believe this should do the trick,

14:53.680 --> 14:56.470
﻿but if it begins to hurt more, .please go to a hospital.

14:56.970 --> 14:57.930
Thank you.

14:57.930 --> 15:00.810
I never would have thought that you had some knowledge of medicine.

15:00.810 --> 15:02.190
Ah, it was ﻿nothing...

15:02.560 --> 15:04.610
﻿I'm really sorry.

15:04.610 --> 15:06.900
﻿Because I took my eyes off of him for a moment...

15:06.900 --> 15:10.450
It's my fault for asking her to take me on a stroll.

15:10.450 --> 15:11.860
﻿Mr. Pierrot...

15:13.240 --> 15:16.160
﻿Thank you for saving my Papa!

15:16.160 --> 15:17.140
Y-Yes...

15:19.500 --> 15:21.040
﻿Stefan, you see...

15:22.420 --> 15:23.670
﻿Nadja, let's go!

15:25.960 --> 15:27.670
﻿Please take care.

15:28.340 --> 15:29.420
﻿Thank you!

15:30.760 --> 15:33.640
﻿Why did you go to see Stefan?!

15:33.640 --> 15:34.430
﻿Th-That's...

15:34.430 --> 15:36.970
﻿For what purpose did you do such a thing?!

15:36.970 --> 15:41.640
﻿I wanted to find out from your wife and Stefan what they thought of you...

15:41.640 --> 15:43.520
﻿Mind your own business!

15:43.520 --> 15:44.770
I'm sorry.

15:44.770 --> 15:49.820
﻿But, Stefan told me... that they both still love you even now.

15:50.320 --> 15:53.700
But, why didn't you go back to see them right away?

15:55.950 --> 15:59.040
﻿They were waiting for your return the entire time.

15:59.040 --> 16:02.290
﻿It's because I thought they could be happier if I wasn't there.

16:02.750 --> 16:04.120
﻿There's no way that's true!

16:04.130 --> 16:06.500
﻿It's a matter of fact that families would be much happier together!

16:06.500 --> 16:08.380
﻿What do you know?!

16:08.380 --> 16:11.720
﻿I'm a failure as a husband and a father!

16:12.590 --> 16:13.340
﻿Abel...

16:15.430 --> 16:20.560
﻿By forcing my own ideals on them, I brought misfortune upon them.

16:20.560 --> 16:21.850
﻿Your ideals?

16:22.230 --> 16:24.480
﻿There was no doctor and no money there.

16:24.480 --> 16:28.650
﻿I wanted to save the villagers who couldn't afford to have satisfactory medical care.

16:28.650 --> 16:34.030
﻿But because of that, I had to sell my wife's dresses and even my family became poor.

16:34.030 --> 16:35.860
﻿And even Stefan...

16:36.490 --> 16:41.290
﻿Like you've saved the other people of this village, please save our family too!

16:41.290 --> 16:44.370
﻿You're this child's father!

16:44.370 --> 16:46.880
I ﻿saved Stefan's life from being lost,

16:46.880 --> 16:49.960
﻿but from the after-effects from the illness, he was paralyzed.

16:49.960 --> 16:51.420
﻿Isn't that terrible?

16:53.420 --> 16:54.840
﻿Ah there they are!

16:54.840 --> 16:59.970
﻿Stefan also told me that your wife blamed herself for your leaving.

16:59.970 --> 17:01.600
﻿That she really regretted it.

17:02.680 --> 17:04.560
﻿Please! See them again!

17:04.560 --> 17:06.600
What can I possibly achieve by seeing them now?

17:06.900 --> 17:10.110
﻿Why won't you? Stefan wants to see you!

17:10.480 --> 17:15.200
﻿I'm also looking for my mother, so I understand Stefan's feelings well.

17:17.320 --> 17:21.740
﻿There isn't a day that passes in which I don't think of my mother.

17:23.250 --> 17:27.500
﻿Every time we travel from c-ty to city, I've been praying that somewhere in the audience...

17:27.500 --> 17:30.880
my mother is standing there... watching me...

17:30.880 --> 17:32.420
﻿Every time my eyes meet with a guest that has the same blonde hair,

17:32.420 --> 17:34.670
﻿the same blue eyes as my own

17:34.670 --> 17:37.550
﻿I get so excited and it feels like my heart is about to burst open.

17:38.430 --> 17:40.390
I'm ﻿really such a fool, aren't I?

17:40.390 --> 17:45.230
﻿The fact of it is, she could look like anyone. And the truth of it may be that she abandoned me.

17:45.980 --> 17:47.890
﻿But, I still want to see my mother!

17:48.770 --> 17:51.190
﻿It's the same for Stefan.

17:51.190 --> 17:54.050
﻿Please, Abel! Meet Stefan!

17:54.050 --> 17:55.170
I can't

17:55.700 --> 17:58.200
﻿Why?! Don't you want to see him too?!

17:58.200 --> 18:01.780
﻿Of course I do! There's no way I wouldn't want to!

18:02.490 --> 18:04.240
﻿I want to embrace him with my hands!

18:05.040 --> 18:06.660
﻿Then why don't you?!

18:06.660 --> 18:08.500
﻿What will meeting him now achieve?

18:08.920 --> 18:13.590
﻿My wife's remarried with someone rich. Both Mary and Stefan are now living in happiness!

18:14.130 --> 18:18.260
﻿If I just casually walked up to them now, what would happen to that happiness?

18:18.260 --> 18:19.260
﻿But...

18:19.760 --> 18:23.310
﻿I don't want to destroy their happiness.

18:24.020 --> 18:26.560
﻿I just want to gently leave them alone as they are now.

18:28.310 --> 18:31.860
﻿But, to leave it at that... is just too sad!

18:31.860 --> 18:37.530
﻿If my mother thinks the same way you do, that would just be too sad!

18:40.820 --> 18:41.660
﻿Nadja...

18:42.280 --> 18:43.490
Go on and meet him.

18:47.040 --> 18:48.370
﻿Master...

18:48.370 --> 18:53.540
﻿Abel, your son has grown up healthy. Go and properly meet him face-to-face.

18:54.210 --> 18:55.170
﻿But...

18:55.170 --> 18:57.920
﻿Abel, you're a pierrot.

18:57.920 --> 19:01.380
﻿As a pierrot, don't you think you can meet him just fine that way?

19:09.350 --> 19:13.310
﻿Next up, here's the entrance of our kind pierrot!

19:23.240 --> 19:26.160
﻿O-O-Oops!

19:33.130 --> 19:33.920
﻿Huh?

19:36.670 --> 19:38.960
﻿T-That's the nutcracker doll!

19:46.350 --> 19:48.560
Wow, amazing!

19:54.310 --> 19:56.110
﻿Thank you for yesterday.

19:56.110 --> 19:58.570
Thanks a lot, Mr. Pierrot!

19:58.650 --> 20:01.440
﻿Thank you very much for taking care of my husband and son.

20:05.740 --> 20:07.370
﻿Th-This is for me?

20:09.870 --> 20:12.330
﻿Oh, it's a nutcracker doll!

20:13.920 --> 20:16.130
﻿Isn't that great, Stefan?

20:16.130 --> 20:16.880
﻿Yeah!

20:17.250 --> 20:21.260
﻿Hey, look! The faces on this doll look just like us!

20:21.260 --> 20:22.920
﻿Ah, you're right.

20:22.930 --> 20:24.680
﻿My! They do, they do.

20:25.180 --> 20:27.550
﻿Mr. Pierrot, thank you!

20:28.060 --> 20:31.620
﻿You better listen to what your mother and father say!

20:37.420 --> 20:41.340
﻿You better listen to what your mother and father say!

20:42.950 --> 20:44.070
﻿Dear...

20:55.540 --> 20:57.290
﻿Mom, what's the matter?

20:58.040 --> 20:59.960
﻿Th-There's just some dust that got into my eye...

21:03.970 --> 21:08.800
﻿That night, Abel performed his perfect pierrot show without showing a single tear.

21:09.350 --> 21:15.390
﻿But, I really understood how much Abel loved his family so much that it hurt.

21:16.770 --> 21:22.820
﻿Director, I will believe that my Mother also loves me as much as Abel loves his family.

21:23.440 --> 21:26.950
﻿And I will continue to believe that someday I will be able to see her.

21:28.320 --> 21:30.950
﻿Hey, everyone! Listen up!

21:30.950 --> 21:33.080
﻿We've decided where we'll be going next!

21:33.080 --> 21:34.580
﻿Where, where?

21:34.960 --> 21:38.080
﻿Nadja, I heard from Abel.

